With --disable-background-networking, avoid CfT Optimization Guide startup when
the configured required-component list is empty. Without that switch, preserve
eager bootstrap. Keep nonempty-list provisioning and required-component waits;
model service entrypoints can still create the global state on demand.

Honor --disable-background-networking at the periodic scheduler, not at component
registration. Registration also loads preinstalled CRLSet, PKI and Safe Browsing
data. Keep those registration and ComponentReady paths unchanged. Required
components and explicit on-demand updates bypass this scheduler and retain their
existing foreground UpdateClient::Update path. The existing
--disable-component-update registration behavior is unchanged.

Timer scheduler regression covers both enabled and disabled periodic checks and
Stop() with mock time. Tests/build/applicability checks were not run here.

Source trace (paths relative to source base):
- chrome/browser/chrome_for_testing/prefs.cc:25-33 registers the empty list.
- chrome/browser/chrome_for_testing/config.cc:249-268 reads the list without
  allocation and supplies the updater's required components.
- chrome/browser/component_updater/chrome_component_updater_configurator.cc:
  325-328 forwards required components to the update service.
- chrome/browser/optimization_guide/model_execution/
  optimization_guide_global_state.cc:108-113 constructs ManifestBrokerState.
- components/optimization_guide/core/model_execution/manifest_broker/
  manifest_broker_state.cc:55-78 constructs ManifestMonitor, whose
  manifest_monitor.cc:72-74 subscribes to the installer delegate.
- chrome/browser/component_updater/
  optimization_guide_on_device_model_installer.cc:278-285,366-389 registers the
  manifest and requests a foreground on-demand update, independently of the
  ordinary RegisterComponentsForUpdate call.
- components/component_updater/component_updater_service.cc:175-188,232-245,
  380-433,436-468 separates periodic scheduling from required-component and
  explicit on-demand UpdateClient::Update calls.
- components/component_updater/component_installer.cc:510-522,594-626 loads
  preinstalled data and calls ComponentReady independently of periodic updates.
- chrome/browser/optimization_guide/optimization_guide_keyed_service.h:332-338
  lazily creates global state; the corresponding .cc:241-260,513-520 retains
  BindModelBroker/CreateModelBrokerClient/StartSession demand entrypoints.

